WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.372
The applied challenge returns the two longest completed stays per department.

00:00:04.372 --> 00:00:09.582
The CTE calculates stay days and assigns ROW_NUMBER within each department.

00:00:09.582 --> 00:00:12.992
Stay duration descending defines the main order.

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:16.502
Admission ID breaks exact duration ties.

00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:20.357
The outer query keeps row numbers one and two.

00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:25.492
After running it, explain why admission-level detail is preserved.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:31.777
Connect this idea to an operations team comparing each event with the previous and next event.

00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:37.477
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:45.152
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.152 --> 00:00:50.722
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:50.722 --> 00:00:56.684
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
